Subject: [PATCH] tu: mark dynamic descriptor sizes of empty shaders unknown

tu_emit_program_state() merges dynamic_descriptor_sizes[] from all
stages, accepting any non-negative value. Empty TCS/TES/GS shaders
start with zeroed metadata, so they claim that every set has zero
dynamic descriptor size and overwrite sizes from real shaders.

With graphics pipeline libraries and independent sets, a fragment
shader that loads its dynamic descriptor base from the driver UBO
then gets the wrong base and can read another set's dynamic buffer.

Mark every entry unknown (-1) in tu_empty_shader_create(), matching
tu_empty_fs_create(). Empty shaders have no layout information and
must not contribute authoritative zeros to the merge.

A840 CTS independent-set tests change from 12 Fail to 480/480 Pass.
The 20% pipeline-library selection (23692 tests) and dynamic
binding-model selection (7262 tests) have 0 Fail.

Fixes failures in the following CTS test family:
dEQP-VK.pipeline.pipeline_library.graphics_library.independent_sets_random.fast_lib.{vert_frag,vert_tesc_tese_frag}.case_{1,4,5,8}*

